AGAINST THE SUPERSEDED T8_MAXDIM64 ROW (2,481,925.71, QD=8 export c169b807):
+14.2% cell area, sequential cells +14.5%, combinational +13.4%, while Vitis
reports FF +0.9% (43,911 -> 44,303) for the same pair of exports.

That gap -- 14.2% of standard-cell area against 0.9% of flip-flops -- is NOT a
measurement of the QD=8-to-16 cost, and must not be quoted as one. The two
exports differ by two days of commits (c169b807 to 92f0618f), not by QD alone, so
this bounds the cost from above and no more. Isolating it needs one export per QD
from the same allo commit, which nobody has run.

What it does say, with the same caveat, is that the FPGA resource table and the
standard-cell area disagree in the same direction as everywhere else in this
project: +0.9% FF against +14.2% area. It is the third instance -- after the
dual-write-port RAM that is free on block RAM and impossible in standard cells,
and MAXDIM 16->64 costing +2.4% FF against +64.1% area.

Non-combinational share 80.1%, against 79.9% on the superseded row and ~80% in
every TinyTPU run so far, so the flop-heavy shape is unchanged.
